1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
What's this for?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,978
Just because. How's the baby?

3
00:00:04,978 --> 00:00:05,956
Fast asleep.

4
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
I'm sorry I missed him. I had to work late.

5
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
What are the flowers for, Richard?

6
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:15,736
Five years of happiness. Happy anniversary.

7
00:00:15,736 --> 00:00:19,068
But our anniversary isn't until Saturday.

8
00:00:19,068 --> 00:00:20,268
I couldn't wait.

9
00:00:20,268 --> 00:00:23,824
Besides, we are not going to be here Saturday.

10
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:25,157
We're not?

11
00:00:25,157 --> 00:00:27,149
Uh-uh.

12
00:00:27,149 --> 00:00:30,411
Where are we going to be?

13
00:00:30,411 --> 00:00:34,238
If you had your choice of all the places in the world.

14
00:00:34,238 --> 00:00:38,714
where would you choose to spend our anniversary?

15
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:39,948
The Watermill Inn.

16
00:00:39,948 --> 00:00:43,212
I loved that place when we went on our honeymoon.

17
00:00:43,212 --> 00:00:46,669
Perfect! You picked the right place.

18
00:00:46,669 --> 00:00:48,017
I don't understand.

19
00:00:48,017 --> 00:00:49,867
You and I, Mrs. Stewart,

20
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:53,603
are going to spend a second honeymoon at the Watermill Inn.

21
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:57,081
Oh, Richard! That's wonderful, but--

22
00:00:57,081 --> 00:00:58,081
No buts.

23
00:00:58,081 --> 00:01:00,059
What about the baby?

24
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:02,059
Aren't we taking the baby on our honeymoon?

25
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:02,537
Absolutely not.

26
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
The world's greatest grandmother, Mrs. Ellen Stewart,

27
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,493
has agreed to take care of him for the weekend.

28
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:12,767
Richard, isn't that too much to ask of your mother?

29
00:01:12,767 --> 00:01:15,529
Too much? She loves taking care of Max.

30
00:01:15,529 --> 00:01:20,405
But ... I'll miss him.

31
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:22,072
Well, we'll phone every hour,

32
00:01:22,072 --> 00:01:25,683
and you can listen to him over the phone.

33
00:01:25,683 --> 00:01:26,361
Come on, Mar.

34
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
It's time you and I had a romantic weekend alone together.

35
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:33,817
We've earned it. What do you say?

36
00:01:33,817 --> 00:01:38,273
It does sound tempting.

37
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:44,341
You're right. We've earned it.

38
00:01:44,341 --> 00:01:47,207
Great! I'll make a reservation right now.

39
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,717
Remember that wonderful little balcony

40
00:01:49,717 --> 00:01:50,185
where we had our meals ...

41
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,563
with a view of the Hudson River?

42
00:01:53,563 --> 00:02:05,074
How could I forget?

43
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:08,052
Hello. Is Mrs. Montefiore there?

44
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,030
Ah. She's out.

45
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,394
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

46
00:02:12,394 --> 00:02:16,986
My wife and I spent our honeymoon at the inn.

47
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:18,814
No, we didn't leave anything in the room.

48
00:02:18,814 --> 00:02:19,964
It's five years ago.

49
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:22,942
We'd like to make a reservation for this weekend.

50
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:28,898
Yes, a double room, please. What?

51
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:35,801
Are you sure? But ... OK.

52
00:02:35,801 --> 00:02:38,232
Nothing available.

53
00:02:38,232 --> 00:02:39,832
Wait! Don't hang up!

54
00:02:39,832 --> 00:02:43,788
Can you recommend someplace nice--someplace nearby?

55
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:52,722
Uh--hold it. Old Country Inn?

56
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:58,678
Right. And the phone number?

57
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:04,634
555-2420. Thank you. 555-2420

58
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,932
He says there's another inn

59
00:03:07,932 --> 00:03:10,589
just half a mile down the road from the Watermill.

60
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
It won't be the same, but what do you say?

61
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:19,567
Well ...

62
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:19,767
My mom is available to baby-sit this weekend.

63
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:21,523
Well, OK. See if they have a room.

64
00:03:21,523 --> 00:03:28,457
Right!

65
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:32,935
Hello. Is this the Old Country Inn?

66
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:34,849
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

67
00:03:34,849 --> 00:03:37,391
The desk clerk at the Watemill suggested your inn.

68
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:39,891
Would you happen to have a room for two availbale

69
00:03:39,891 --> 00:03:41,369
this weekend?

70
00:03:41,369 --> 00:03:42,569
Something really nice.

71
00:03:42,569 --> 00:03:44,903
My wife and I are celebrating our fifth anniversary.

72
00:03:44,903 --> 00:03:52,281
Yes. I'll hold. He's checking. You do?

73
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:54,852
Great! What is the daily rate?

74
00:03:54,852 --> 00:03:57,389
That's fine. Thank you.

75
00:03:57,389 --> 00:04:03,375
Yes, we'll be arriving by car about ten o'clock Friday night.

76
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:14,834
Stewart. S-t-e-w-a-r-t. Thank you.

77
00:04:14,834 --> 00:04:17,405
Done! You and I, Mrs. Stewart.

78
00:04:17,405 --> 00:04:25,038
are going to have a wonderful, romantic weekend!

79
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,038
Richard, that's the baby. Richard
